text:
{
"opening": "This release introduces new locale support for Albanian, Tamil, and Zulu, enhancing internationalization capabilities. It also improves parser validation and extends the `dehumanize` functionality to additional locales.",
"requirements": [
{
"id": "m03",
"text": "The library must expose a public class named `ZuluLocale` that provides localization support for the Zulu language."
},
{
"id": "m04",
"text": "The library must expose a public class named `TamilLocale` that provides localization support for the Tamil language."
},
{
"id": "m06",
"text": "The `DateTimeParser` must enforce stricter validation when processing tokens 'A' and 'hh', raising appropriate errors for invalid inputs."
},
{
"id": "m14",
"text": "The release must ensure that the `MoroccoArabicLocale` is available and correctly integrated into the locale system."
},
{
"id": "m15",
"text": "The library must expose a public class named `AlbanianLocale` that provides localization support for the Albanian language."
},
{
"id": "m20",
"text": "The `FinnishLocale` must be refactored to correctly support the `dehumanize` function for Finnish date formatting."
},
{
"id": "m21",
"text": "The `ArrowFactory` must accept `Decimal` instances as input arguments for the `get` method, treating them as timestamps."
},
{
"id": "m25",
"text": "The `dehumanize` method on the `Arrow` object must correctly generate human-readable negative time strings for Estonian, Finnish, Nepali, and Zulu locales."
}
],
"closing": "Please verify that all new locales are properly registered and that existing locale behaviors remain unchanged except where specified."
}
